# adocs/data/S154_floor_margin_sweep.py, every mode, run at fc5526e on the
# machine .moltke.local.md describes, 2026-09-01. What it settles:
#
#   1. The comment beside MATE_IN_THREE_FLOOR claimed the floor "fails when the
#      guard fails and not when the tree shifts underneath it" and asserted it.
#      Measured: the count moves by 0 positions over the seventeen commits that
#      touched src/ since the floor was placed, and by 0 over nine table sizes
#      from 1 MB to 256 MB. One ply of the guard itself moves five. The claim
#      is true and is now a number.
#
#   2. The floor of 7 had stopped separating. S145 placed it between 8 shipping
#      and 6 with the guard removed. S165 lifted both ends to 9 and 7, so
#      `7 >= 7` was green with the guard gone and the assertion could no longer
#      fail for the reason it exists -- from 2026-08-23 until this run. The
#      floor is 8 now, and the `red` block below is that failing as it must.
#
#   3. S145's log and step file characterise the RfpMinPly 1 row of the
#      mate-in-two set as "13 of 16". The assertion also requires
#      `first_exact == 2m - 1`, so what it fails there is 7 positions and not 3:
#      9 of 16 are found on time. The `floor` block prints both numbers, and the
#      `red` block's run of the real gate logs the seven by name.
#
# The engine is driven over UCI with the standard library alone; the set's
# distances were proved once by S145's two oracles and are read from the TSV.
# `git worktree` is used for every build and the tracked tree is never edited.
# -Werror is dropped in those worktrees because pre-S167 commits do not compile
# under Apple clang; it changes no codegen.

